<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Cieza de León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1520–1554</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Cieza de León was a Spanish soldier and chronicler who spent some seventeen years in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> from 1535. His Chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, the first part of which was published in 1553, describes the geography, peoples and history of the Andes and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>, drawing on interviews with Inca nobles. It is one of the most important early sources for Inca history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-cieza-de-leon.jpg" alt="Pedro Cieza de León" width="192" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_Cieza_de_Le%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
